  "rule": "A2 split-head rule (second experiment of candidate A2, phase 2d), written 2026-11-01T15:49:42+07:00 before any A2 split-head model is built. Not from a source. Not reviewed by the user (user request of 2026-11-01 to finish the remaining unknowns, the earlier A2 rule allowed this experiment only if the first left the question open, it did not, this is a new rule with a new reason). Reviewed by the advisor (inventory results/notes/phase2e_unknowns_inventory.md).\nQuestion: A2 default export (decode in the INT8 graph, no DFL) lost 12.58 pp from FP16 to INT8 and could not separate the INT8 quantization of the ltrb conv output from the decode arithmetic (rule_nodfl.txt, page 15 section 4). If the ltrb output and the class logits are exported raw (split head, decode on the CPU in numpy) does the INT8 model meet the FP16 accuracy?\nModel and method: ppe5_yolov8n_nodfl_100ep_s0 weights/best.pt, build_split.py (two raw outputs boxes 1x4x8400 ltrb distances and scores 1x5x8400 logits, decode_split with reg_max inferred from the box channels, tests/test_split_head.py), INT8 with the calibration list of baseline seed 0 (dataset.txt of ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_100ep_s0, the same as every INT8 export), FP16 build for the control. Evaluated through the board dump path with metadata split_head true (evaluate.py --backend rknn --variant split).\nValidity controls (read before any INT8 number), same as A1: V-PC decode_split of the exported ONNX against output0 of the standard weights/best.onnx (onnxruntime, random input) at most 0.01, V-board the split FP16 model has css_test AP50-95 within 1.35 pp of the standard FP16 of A2 (49.33). If a control fails no INT8 result is read.\nStatements (css_test, AP50-95, AP NoHelmet, AP Vest, pp): N2-1 A2 split INT8 minus A2 split FP16, minus A2 standard FP16 (49.33), minus A2 default INT8 (36.75). 'meets' when AP50-95 is at least 47.98 (A2 standard FP16 minus 1.35, the criterion of rule_split.txt, new and unreviewed). N2-2 reading, fixed now: meets -> the INT8 quantization of the ltrb conv output and class logits is not the main source of the loss, the arithmetic tail of the decode is implicated, the same reading as A1 without DFL. Does not meet -> the INT8 quantization of the ltrb conv output (or class logits) is implicated for A2, which A1 did not show for the DFL logits. Meets or not, no mechanism is named. N2-3 dtype counts and CPU rows of the layer table of the INT8 build.\nLimits: one seed, one run, A2 is a different model (random box branch, page 15), the split build is one build. NPU time and decode time are not measured (A1 measured them under P2, the box output is 4 channels instead of 64 so the decode cost differs and is unknown). Budget: one build per precision and one evaluation each, one experiment.\n\nADDENDUM 2026-11-01T16:07:10+07:00: the first evaluation attempt crashed on the board before any result (the board still had the old split_decode.py with a fixed reg_max 16, ValueError cannot reshape array of size 33600 into shape (1,4,16,8400)), fixed by make board-sync of the generalized decode. The builds and V-PC are unchanged. The evaluations are rerun, no rule statement changed.\n"
