  "rule": "QAT NPU time and coverage rule (item 'Th\u1eddi gian NPU v\u00e0 \u0111\u1ed9 ph\u1ee7 \u0111a nh\u00e2n c\u1ee7a b\u1ea3n QAT' of results/notes/phase2e_unknowns_inventory.md, left outside the budget of rule_qat.txt), written 2026-11-01T16:09:41+07:00 before any QAT latency exists. Not from a source. Not reviewed by the user (request of 2026-11-01). Reviewed by the advisor (inventory). Same statements, approved numbers (5 percent, 2 session gap rule) and protocol P2 (NOT approved, page 16) as onboard_q2j/rule.txt. Models of ppe5_yolov8n_baseline_100ep_s0 (sha256):\n  rknn_int8h5 80be7f5d6adaa091b5b706f24052f97218dbbcda39e28d3ab2034e812cc24938\n  rknn_int8_split 8b0a753198b82f1a7ce2e8c2569dbf3b32d40c71ea19d1c999ae02a42390e26b\n  rknn_int8_qat 9e5def19242b1b910cce5f343c0d5a8535c620d99128b0b1bed47bd8dbb19441\nDesign: one interleaved P2 run, SiLU seed 0 only, conditions int8h5, split INT8 (A1), QAT (benchmark_npu.py --precision int8 --variant qat), for mask in CORE_0, CORE_0_1_2, 2 sessions per condition, same order in both rounds, 45 s rest, helper x4_hold.sh in pin mode, driver aborts if a model file changes. Statements: Q-T1 NPU time = median of the two session medians for each condition and mask, QAT against split INT8 and against int8h5 in ms and percent with the session gap rule (a change is 'kh\u00e1c' only when at least 5 percent and larger than the larger session gap, else 'kh\u00f4ng ph\u00e2n bi\u1ec7t \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c'). Q-T2 total time of QAT = its NPU time at CORE_0 plus the CPU decode median of A1 (8.02 ms, experiments/npu/operator_support/onboard_q2j/decode_bench.json, the QAT output tensors have the same shapes 1x64x8400 and 1x5x8400 as A1, the decode of QAT itself is not re-measured), compared with the NPU time of int8h5. Q-T3 coverage: share of the QAT CORE_0_1_2 session cycles in rows with at least two cores above 0 percent of WorkLoad, against the cycles of the same session table (criterion 50 percent of the approved gate A, used for d